From 1ba0bb111d2903bad559accb7599e0ef1c00de26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: therealjkvalentine <lab@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:11:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LFB profiler (OGL_LFB_PROF), faster write-only unlock, GL 1.2
 extension check, MSVC + mingw build scripts

- lfbprof.cpp/.h: per-frame CPU timing of grLfbLock/grLfbUnlock/grBufferSwap, off unless OGL_LFB_PROF is set.
- grLfbUnlock (write-only): skip colour-key-only rows two pixels per compare, convert only rows with written
  pixels, upload only the written columns (GL_UNPACK_ROW_LENGTH). OGL_LFB_FAST=0 restores the stock loop.
  The write-only lock never read back the frame buffer; the cost was the full-buffer scan and upload.
- GLExtensions: GL_EXT_packed_pixels / GL_EXT_bgra are core in GL 1.2; accept them so macOS legacy contexts
  (GL_APPLE_packed_pixels) do not raise a modal warning at boot.
- build-msvc.ps1 (VS 2019 x86, /MT, CPPDLL exports) and build-mingw.sh (i686 mingw-w64, macOS/Linux/w64devkit).
---
 GLExtensions.cpp |   8 ++-
 build-hd.ps1     |   2 +-
 build-mingw.sh   |  19 ++++++
